  "title": "CSRF XSS CSP injection SSRF open redirects and clickjacking",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "concepts": [
    "Attacks target separate trust boundaries: browser state-changing requests, HTML and script contexts, server queries, outbound network requests, and navigations. Controls must match the boundary.",
    "Output encoding must match the browser context; sanitization is for intentionally accepted markup. CSP is defense in depth and cannot replace safe rendering or context-aware encoding.",
    "CSRF exploits ambient browser credentials, while XSS executes attacker-controlled code in the trusted origin. Cookie attributes and antiforgery tokens reduce CSRF exposure but do not neutralize XSS.",
    "SSRF defense requires destination allowlists, DNS and IP checks, redirect handling, and network egress controls; validating a raw URL string alone is insufficient."
  ],
